  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "The values of functions $q(x)$ and $r(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=0$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $q(x)$ | $r(x)$ | ${q}^{\u2032}(x)$ | ${r}^{\u2032}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $-1$ | $3$ | $2$ | $-1$ |\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3q(x)+4r(x))$ at $x=0.$\n\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3q(x)+4r(x))|}_{x=0}=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Using the sum and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3q(x)+4r(x))=3{q}^{\u2032}(x)+4{r}^{\u2032}(x).\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=0$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3q(x)+4r(x))|}_{x=0} & =3{q}^{\u2032}(0)+4{r}^{\u2032}(0) \\\\  & =3(2)+4(-1) \\\\  & =6-4 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
